    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0066]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0070" num="0066" class="description-line">Manufacture of Anode</div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0067]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0071" num="0067" class="description-line">96 weight % of carbon powder as an anode active material, 3 weight % of polyvinylidene fluoride (PVdF) as a binding agent, and 1 weight % of carbon black as a conductive material were added to N-methyl-2 pyrrolidone (NMP) as a solvent, to prepare an anode mix slurry. The anode mix slurry was applied to a copper (Cu) foil as an anode current collector having 10 μm thickness, followed by drying, to manufacture an anode, which was roll-pressed.</div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0068]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0072" num="0068" class="description-line">Manufacture of Cathode</div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0069]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0073" num="0069" class="description-line">92 weight % of lithium cobalt composite oxide as a cathode active material, 4 weight % of carbon black as a conductive material, and 4 weight % of PVdF as a binding agent were added to N-methyl-2 pyrrolidone (NMP) as a solvent, to prepare a cathode mix slurry. The cathode mix slurry was applied to an aluminum (Al) foil as a cathode current collector having 20 μm thickness, followed by drying, to manufacture a cathode, which was roll-pressed.</div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0070]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0074" num="0070" class="description-line">Fabrication of Battery</div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0071]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0075" num="0071" class="description-line">Batteries were fabricated by assembling the manufactured electrodes and the manufactured separators using a stacking method, and by injecting an electrolyte in the assembled result, the electrolyte being ethylene carbonate (EC)/ethyl methyl carbonate (EMC)=½ (volumetric ratio) and 1 mole of lithium hexafluorophosphate (LiPF<sub>6</sub>).</div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0072]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0076" num="0072" class="description-line">A hot box test and a cycle performance test at 60° C. were carried out on the fabricated batteries, and the test results are shown in Tables 3 and 4.</div>
    </li> <li> <div id="p-0077" num="0000" class="description-line">
      <tables id="TABLE-US-00003" num="00003">
